From: aleks2 (H37)
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] messages: no thread-local buffer

A loaded mod has no thread-local storage on Switch: the dynamic loader refuses a module
with PT_TLS, and this thread_local std::vector was the only one in Randomizer. Message text
is resolved on the game thread only, so one static buffer serves the same purpose.
---
diff --git a/src/messages.cpp b/src/messages.cpp
index 0bc2e7a..37c51b8 100644
--- a/src/messages.cpp
+++ b/src/messages.cpp
@@ -189,7 +189,10 @@ bool formatted_override(
         return false;
     }
 
-    thread_local std::vector<uint8_t> formatted;
+    // aleks2 (H37): one buffer, not thread_local. Message text is resolved on the game thread
+    // only, and a loaded mod has no thread-local storage on Switch: the dynamic loader refuses a
+    // module with PT_TLS. The text must stay valid until the next call, which it does.
+    static std::vector<uint8_t> formatted;
     formatted = encoded_text(fmt::format(fmt::runtime(textIt->second), value));
     outText->text = formatted.data();
     outText->text_size = formatted.size();
